        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Thimble-shaped bag of fine silk canvas embroidered with coloured silks in tent stitch. The top is joined to a crochet border of greyish-beige silk through which is run a draw string of twisted beige silk. The bottom is gathered into a crochet roundel of the same silk and is decorated with a silk tassel. A line of brown silk marks the base of the bag. It is lined with yellow silk. On both sides is the same pastoral scene of a shepherdess with her sheep. A border of interlaced sprays of oak leaves and acorns decorates the upper part of the bag and single sprays of acorns and leaves decorates the lower part. The ground is unworked."@en , "Bag of embroidered silk canvas, France, ca. 1820"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/ad0cbbe1-0270-3ef6-a8da-2d11b4e5e5c0> ;
